// Strmm performs the triangular matrix-matrix multiplication.
//
// C={αop(A)Bif side == [SideLeft]αBop(A)if side == [SideRight]
// where A is a triangular matrix stored in lower or upper mode with or without the main diagonal, B and C are m×n matrix, and α is a scalar. Also, for matrix A
// op(A)={Aif transa == CUBLAS_OP_NAᵀif transa == CUBLAS_OP_TAᴴif transa == [OpC]
// Notice that in order to achieve better parallelism cuBLAS differs from the BLAS API only for this routine. The BLAS API assumes an in-place implementation (with results written back to B), while the cuBLAS API assumes an out-of-place implementation (with results written into C). The application can obtain the in-place functionality of BLAS in the cuBLAS API by passing the address of the matrix B in place of the matrix C. No other overlapping in the input parameters is supported.
// For references please refer to NETLIB documentation:
// strmm(), dtrmm(), ctrmm(), ztrmm()
//
// [Handle.Strmm64] takes 64-bit sizes.
//
//   - side: Indicates if matrix A is on the left or right of B
//   - uplo: Indicates if matrix A lower or upper part is stored, the other part is not referenced and is inferred from the stored elements
//   - trans: Operation op( A) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - diag: Indicates if the elements on the main diagonal of matrix A are unity and should not be accessed
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix B, with matrix A sized accordingly
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix B, with matrix A sized accordingly
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication, if alpha == 0 then A is not referenced and B does not have to be a valid input
//   - a: < type > array of dimension lda x m with lda >= max(1, m) if side == [SideLeft] and lda x n with lda >= max(1, n) otherwise
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - b: < type > array of dimension ldb x n with ldb >= max(1, m)
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix B
//   - c: < type > array of dimension ldc x n with ldc >= max(1, m)
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix C
//
// Returns:
//   - [ErrExecutionFailed]: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: - If m < 0, n < 0, or - if trans is not one of [OpN], [OpT] and [OpC], or - if uplo is not one of [FillModeLower] and [FillModeUpper], or - if side is not one of [SideLeft] and [SideRight], or - if lda < max(1, m) if side == [SideLeft], and lda < max(1, n) otherwise, or - if ldb < max(1, m), or - if ldc < max(1, m), or - if alpha is NULL
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized
//   - [Success]: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasStrmm_v2.
func (h Handle) Strmm(side SideMode, uplo FillMode, trans Operation, diag DiagType, m int32, n int32, alpha *float32, a driver.DevicePtr, lda int32, b driver.DevicePtr, ldb int32, c driver.DevicePtr, ldc int32) error {
	return strmm(h, side, uplo, trans, diag, m, n, alpha, a, lda, b, ldb, c, ldc)
}

